-	<!-- custom: the more i learn the more i am upset about how usa-centric and appalingly forgetful it is sometimes, if not blatantly propagandist, even though rare, but for example see the ecology entry vs new one from wikipedia but anyways etc, the base civ4 +/- advciv version seems to totally obscure i mean anyways etc the fact that the mount was stolen from the indigenous people that was there, i mean technically it wasn't "there's" per se as it belongs to nature i.e. anyone that can control it, still glorifying it without any mention of past owner is simply disgusting, but anyways etc, hopefully some truth is restored even though i didn't know at all before and barely looked now whiel reworking this building but anyways etc, hopefully this is not a too widespread problem in civ4 and i fixed some entries but anyways etc ; nevermind it's even more disgusting that i thought, with lines like "remarkably, no one was killed during construction", i wonder who even wrote those fucking lines??? If this is is not self-glorifying propaganda, but anyways etc, i am glad i learned the "truth" if i may say even though it is relative to one's point of view whatever that means, but my view of it is this is disgustingly concealed if i may say but anyways etc, entry now from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Rushmore anyways etc -->
